    LLM: 'Game: Two Hundred. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '200 (Deux Cents) is a point-trick partnership card game from Canada, especially popular in New Brunswick. Four players use a 36-card deck (2s, 3s, 4s, 6s removed). Teams bid in increments of 5 (50-100); highest bidder names trump and must make their bid. First team to 200 points wins.',
    objective: 'First partnership to reach 200 points wins. Bid for the right to name trump; make your bid to score, or lose the amount.',
    gameplay: 'Bidding (50-100 in 5s); highest bidder declares trump and leads. Follow suit; highest trump or led-suit card wins trick. Aces 10 pts, 10s 10 pts, 5s 5 pts (100 pts per deal).',
